course: dictionary
lesson: 13928
title: The legislative branch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Legislative is a long word, but it is built from parts you can learn. Legis means law, and -ative means having to do with. So legislative means to do with making laws. «The legislative work of the country happens in the parliament building.» The words legislative work tell you the job is making laws.
explain: Look for clue words around it. «Our class council agreed on new rules, but only the legislative group can make them official.» The words rules and make them official are clues. Legislative is about making rules that become laws. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Making laws would fit, so you are on the right track.
explain: Government has three branches, and each has its own job. The legislative branch makes laws, the executive branch carries them out, and the judicial branch judges them. «The executive branch put the new law into action, and the judges checked that it was fair.» Learning which job goes with which word helps you remember them all.
fact: Legislative means to do with making laws.
fact: The legislative branch of government is the part, such as Parliament or Congress, that makes laws.
fact: Legis is a root meaning law, and -ative means having to do with, so legislative means having to do with laws.
fact: The three branches of government are legislative (makes laws), executive (carries them out) and judicial (judges them).
fact: «The legislative branch passed a new law about school lunches.» Here legislative tells you which branch made the law.
exercise: «The legislative branch met on Monday to vote on a new law.» What does legislative mean here? | To do with cooking food | To do with growing plants | To do with sports and games | *To do with making laws
exercise: Which branch of government makes the laws? | *Legislative | Musical | Judicial | Executive
exercise: Find and copy the word that means to do with making laws. «The legislative group met to talk about new rules.» | met | group | rules | *legislative
test: «Parliament is part of the legislative branch, because it makes laws.» What does legislative mean? | To do with eating | To do with running fast | *To do with making laws | To do with weather
test: In a government, which branch carries out the laws? | Legislative | Judicial | *Executive | Musical
exam: Which word means to do with making laws? | *Legislative | Judicial | Executive | Electrical
